        "## Categories\n\n### 1. Catheter-related (most common)\n- UVC, UAC, PICC, CVC\n- Femoral, subclavian, IJ veins\n- 1-3 % с indwelling catheters\n- Often asymptomatic (detected on echo / Doppler)\n\n### 2. Renal vein thrombosis\n- ELBW, polycythemia, dehydration, IDM\n- Presentation: hematuria, palpable abdominal mass, thrombocytopenia\n- US: enlarged echogenic kidney, absent venous flow\n\n### 3. Arterial thromboembolism\n- Aortic (UAC-related)\n- Peripheral (rare)\n- Iliac / femoral (catheter complication)\n\n### 4. Cerebral sinovenous thrombosis\n- See art-stroke\n\n## Risk factors\n\n### Maternal\n- Diabetes (IDM)\n- Preeclampsia\n- Antiphospholipid syndrome\n- Maternal infection / sepsis\n\n### Neonatal\n- Indwelling catheters\n- Sepsis\n- Polycythemia (HCT > 65)\n- Dehydration\n- Prothrombotic disorders (Factor V Leiden, prothrombin G20210A)\n- Congenital cardiac (especially Fontan, BT shunt)\n\n## Diagnostics\n\n- **Doppler ultrasound** — first-line vessels\n- **Echo** — intracardiac, IVC tip\n- **Venogram** — gold standard (rare у newborn — radiation)\n- **MRV** — cerebral, renal\n- **Coagulation panel + thrombophilia screen** (selected cases)\n\n## Treatment (decisions individualized)\n\n### Conservative (asymptomatic catheter-related)\n- Remove catheter ASAP\n- Monitor с serial Doppler\n- Most resolve spontaneously\n\n### Anticoagulation (symptomatic, occlusive, large)\n- **Heparin** continuous IV: 28 ед/кг/h, titrate aPTT 60-85 sec\n- **LMWH (enoxaparin)** 1-1.5 мг/кг q12h SC, titrate anti-Xa 0.5-1.0\n- Duration: 6 weeks — 3 months typically\n\n### Thrombolysis (life/limb-threatening)\n- **Alteplase** 0.1-0.5 мг/кг/h IV × 6 ч (limb / organ ischemia)\n- High bleeding risk у newborn — last-resort, ICU + IR\n- Catheter clearance: alteplase 0.5-2 мг intra-luminal\n\n### Avoid\n- Aspirin у newborn (Reye syndrome)\n- Routine anticoagulation у asymptomatic small thrombi\n\n## Calculator Bordik\n- neo-heparin (cont infusion)\n- neo-enoxaparin\n- neo-alteplase-cvc-dose (intra-luminal)\n\n## Источники\n- Monagle P et al. Chest 2012;141:e737S — ACCP Pediatric\n- Saracco P et al. Acta Paediatr 2009;98:1252\n- Albisetti M. Hematology Am Soc Hematol Educ Program 2003",
