        "## Definition\n\nCHI — most common cause persistent neonatal hypoglycemia. Inappropriate insulin secretion при low glucose.\n\n## Genetics\n\n### Channels (most common — 40-60 %)\n- **ABCC8** (SUR1 subunit KATP channel) — autosomal recessive (focal или diffuse)\n- **KCNJ11** (Kir6.2 subunit KATP) — same\n- Diazoxide-unresponsive typically\n\n### Metabolic\n- **GLUD1** (glutamate dehydrogenase) — hyperinsulinism + hyperammonemia syndrome\n- **GCK** (glucokinase) — autosomal dominant\n- **HADH** (3-hydroxyacyl-CoA dehydrogenase)\n- **HNF4A, HNF1A** (transient or permanent)\n- **SLC16A1** (exercise-induced)\n\n### Syndromic\n- **Beckwith-Wiedemann syndrome** — 50 % с hypoglycemia\n- **Sotos syndrome**\n- **Kabuki syndrome**\n\n## Diagnostic criteria\n\n### Critical sample (during hypoglycemia < 2.5 ммоль/л)\n- **Insulin** > 2 µE/мл (inappropriately high)\n- **C-peptide** > 0.5 ng/мл\n- **β-hydroxybutyrate** < 1.5 ммоль/л (suppressed)\n- **Free fatty acids** < 1 ммоль/л (suppressed)\n- Growth hormone normal\n- Cortisol > 18 µg/дл (450 нмоль/л)\n- Ammonia (high in GLUD1)\n\n### Glucagon stimulation test\n- 0.03 мг/кг IM/IV during hypoglycemia\n- Glucose ↑ > 1.6 ммоль/л в 30 мин = positive (CHI characteristic)\n- IEM other → no response\n\n## Treatment hierarchy\n\n### 1. Glucose support\n- D10W bolus 2 мл/кг IV slow (200 мг/кг)\n- Continuous GIR — start 8-10 мг/кг/мин, titrate up до 25-30 if needed\n- Goal glucose > 3.5 ммоль/л\n\n### 2. Diazoxide — first-line CHI\n- 5-15 мг/кг/d split q8h PO\n- Mechanism: opens KATP channels (only effective if channel functional — i.e., not ABCC8/KCNJ11 mutations)\n- Trial 5 days; if responsive, continue chronic\n- Side effects: hirsutism, fluid retention, pulmonary HTN (rare)\n\n### 3. Octreotide (diazoxide-unresponsive)\n- 5-25 мкг/кг/d split q6-8h SC or continuous IV\n- Long-acting somatostatin analog — inhibits insulin release\n- Side effects: NEC concerns (avoid с other risk factors), gallstones long-term\n\n### 4. Other (refractory)\n- Continuous glucose monitoring (CGM)\n- Sirolimus (rare — diffuse CHI selected)\n- Glucagon infusion (short-term bridge)\n\n### 5. Surgical\n- **Genetic testing first** (ABCC8/KCNJ11 mutations)\n- **18F-DOPA PET imaging** — distinguishes focal (single lesion) vs diffuse\n- **Focal CHI:** 95-98 % pancreatectomy curative\n- **Diffuse CHI:** subtotal pancreatectomy (98 %) — high diabetes risk later\n\n## Calculator Bordik\n- neo-glucose-bolus-dose, neo-gir\n- neo-diazoxide-dose, neo-octreotide-dose, neo-glucagon-dose\n\n## Источники\n- Stanley CA. Annu Rev Nutr 2004;24:301\n- De Leon DD et al. J Clin Endocrinol Metab 2009;94:2541\n- Banerjee I et al. Front Endocrinol 2019;10:111",
