        "CATCH-22: Cardiac (TOF, IAA), Abnormal facies, Thymus aplasia (T-cell deficit), Cleft palate, Hypocalcemia. Calcium replacement, IVIG, cardiac surgery.",
        "## Definition\n\n22q11.2 deletion syndrome (also called DiGeorge / VCFS / Shprintzen) — most common deletion syndrome (1/4000-6000 births). Variable phenotype.\n\n## CATCH-22 mnemonic\n\n- **C**ardiac defects (75 %)\n- **A**bnormal facies\n- **T**hymic hypoplasia (T-cell deficiency)\n- **C**left palate\n- **H**ypocalcemia (60-80 %)\n- **22q11.2** deletion\n\n## Cardiac defects (most common)\n\n- **Tetralogy of Fallot** (20 %)\n- **Interrupted aortic arch** type B (50 % of IAA cases)\n- **Truncus arteriosus** (35 % of truncus cases)\n- **VSD** (15 %)\n- **Right aortic arch**\n- **Vascular ring**\n\n## Hypocalcemia\n\n### Mechanism\n- Parathyroid hypoplasia / aplasia → ↓ PTH\n- Ca < 1.75 ммоль/л common\n\n### Treatment\n- **Calcium gluconate 10 % 0.5-1 мл/кг IV slow** acute\n- Continuous infusion 50-200 мг/кг/d Ca gluconate в TPN\n- **Calcitriol** 0.025-0.1 мкг/кг/d PO (active vit D)\n- **Phosphorus restriction** (low-P formula если severe)\n- Lifelong replacement если permanent hypoparathyroidism\n\n## Immunological\n\n### Severity spectrum\n- **Complete DiGeorge** (< 1 %) — absent thymus + T cells; phenotype like SCID\n- **Partial DiGeorge** (>99 %) — variable T-cell numbers, mostly mild\n\n### T-cell function\n- TRECs may be low (newborn screen)\n- Detailed immunology: CD3/4/8 counts, T-cell function (PHA proliferation)\n\n### Treatment severe T-cell deficiency\n- **Reverse-isolation** до immune reconstitution\n- **CMV-negative + irradiated blood products**\n- **Avoid live vaccines** (BCG, MMR, rotavirus)\n- **IVIG monthly** если humoral defect\n- **Pneumocystis prophylaxis** TMP-SMX 5 мг/кг/d\n- **Thymic transplant** — для complete DiGeorge specialist centers (Markert protocol Duke)\n- **HSCT** alternative для complete DiGeorge\n\n## Other features\n\n### Facial\n- Long face\n- Hooded eyelids\n- Bulbous nasal tip\n- Small mouth\n- Mild ear abnormalities\n\n### Cleft palate\n- Submucous cleft common (overt < 10 %)\n- Velopharyngeal incompetence (speech)\n- Nasal regurgitation feeding\n\n### Renal\n- Anomalies (40-50 %)\n- Renal agenesis, dysgenesis, multicystic\n\n### Other\n- Skeletal anomalies\n- Learning disabilities (variable)\n- Psychiatric (schizophrenia ↑ risk adult)\n- Thrombocytopenia (rare)\n\n## Diagnostics\n\n### Confirmation\n- **FISH 22q11.2** (TUPLE1, N25 probes)\n- **Microarray (CMA)** — preferred, finds smaller deletions too\n- **MLPA** — alternative\n\n### Workup at diagnosis\n- **Echocardiogram** (cardiac defects)\n- **Calcium + PTH** (hypoparathyroidism)\n- **CBC + lymphocyte subsets** (T-cell deficiency)\n- **Renal US** (CAKUT)\n- **Cleft palate evaluation** (ENT)\n- **Genetic counseling** (familial recurrence risk)\n\n## Calculator Bordik\n- neo-cagluconate-dose\n- neo-cchd-pulse-oximetry\n- neo-perinatal-infections-class\n\n## Источники\n- McDonald-McGinn DM et al. Nat Rev Dis Primers 2015;1:15071\n- Kobrynski LJ, Sullivan KE. Lancet 2007;370:1443\n- AAP Section on Cardiology 2024",
